Internal D-Bus menu importer
===========================

This directory contains a locally maintained copy of the importer side of
libdbusmenu-qt. It builds the static dbusmenuqt target for Material's application
menus using Qt Widgets and Qt DBus. It does not include a menu exporter.

Provenance
----------

The code was bundled in repository commit dec3fd2b0ba9c0e9cf98dc982da04b4b1577e2ea.
Commit 0277a1d6e127bdaf89955ef18799e42cc07a6189 records a subsequent update from
Plasma Workspace's libdbusmenuqt at f07b7f1c23636e9f1c190971bc6dc371d6b52253:

https://github.com/guiodic/material-decoration/commit/0277a1d6e127bdaf89955ef18799e42cc07a6189
https://github.com/KDE/plasma-workspace/commit/f07b7f1c23636e9f1c190971bc6dc371d6b52253

This is a historical synchronization point, not a release version for the
current copy. The copy has since been ported to Qt 6 and modified locally; its
current behavior is outlined below.
Source-file SPDX notices retain the applicable licensing and attribution.

Local behavior
--------------

- Load one menu level at a time; fetch submenus on demand. An activation request
  for an unknown item first fetches the ID tree, then loads its ancestor menus.
- Reject obsolete asynchronous replies using both the menu instance and its
  request generation, including when an item ID is reused after deletion.
- Restore omitted mutable properties to defaults in complete layouts. Apply
  incremental property signals only to the properties they update or remove.
- Keep KDE section-heading widgets (x-kde-title) synchronized with their actions.
- Handle mnemonic escaping and likely unescaped filename underscores, and retry
  opening empty submenus after their asynchronous contents arrive. Filename
  detection is a compatibility heuristic, not an unambiguous protocol rule.

Limits
------

The importer displays at most 1,000 direct children per menu and keeps at most
5,000 imported actions in total. Layout decoding has a separate, per-tree budget
of 5,001 nodes: the root plus up to 5,000 descendants, shared across all branches.
If decoding stops at this budget, the importer ignores the incomplete layout,
preserves the previous menu, and cancels activation searches based on that tree.
The local truncation flag is not serialized on D-Bus.

These are node/action limits, not byte limits on messages or property values.
Transport validation, including wire nesting limits, is handled by QtDBus/libdbus.

Maintenance and validation
--------------------------

An upstream release alone is not a reason to remove this copy. Before replacing
it, check Qt 6 integration and each local behavior above against the proposed
replacement, port any remaining fixes, and run the importer regression suites.
Record the upstream revision when synchronizing again.

With the project's development dependencies, Qt Test and dbus-run-session
installed, run from the repository root:

    cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON
    cmake --build build --target dbusmenuimporter_test dbusmenustalelayout_test
    ctest --test-dir build -R '^(dbusmenuimporter|dbusmenustalelayout)$' --output-on-failure

CMake registers these tests only when dbus-run-session is found at configuration
time. CTest supplies QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen and an isolated D-Bus session.
